        "abstract": "This paper analyses the transient and steady state behaviour of a three phase induction motor supplied from a current source inverter. It replaces the blocks of stator current by a truncated Fourier series and evaluates the required number of harmonics to use in order to ensure acceptably accurate results. Rectangular as well as trapezoidal blocks of stator current are considered and the results show that the torque pulsations due to trapezoidal current waveforms are smaller than those due to rectangular current waveforms. Commutation circuits in the inverter could therefore be used to ensure required trapezoidal waveforms in order to ensure certain reduced torque pulsations.",
