        "abstract": "The paper describes two phenomena associated with large non-insulated squirrel cage induction motors having a faulty cage. (i) The production of additional time harmonics in the spectrum of the primary current, and (ii) The production of large axial vibrations due to the substantial interbar currents present in non-insulated faulty cages. The combination of these two phenomena forms the basis of a new diagnostic technique for detecting a broken bar and/or endring. Experimentai results are given which verify the viability of this technique.",
