        "abstract": "Messrs Becker and Grayer make mention of the fact that in the machine tested the rotor bar impedance is of the same order as its resistance. They pointed out that this is not the case in the smaller machines that are typically found in a university laboratory and therefore results so obtained and “extrapolated” could be erroneous. The authors recognised that this could be the case and seeing that the emphasis was on large motors, all the measurements and experimental work described in this paper were thus carried out on large motors. However, as shown in reference 1 below, measurements were also performed on smaller laboratory machines and after having accounted for the different orders of the parameters, very good agreement was achieved between theory and measurement.",
