        "abstract": "Prof David H Jacobson, (Deputy President, CSIR). Nonlinear identification and control tasks of considerable magnitude and complexity occur in processes such as the distribution of energy via high-voltage grids, smelting and metal-processing, signal encription and processing, early-warning radar systems, economic-policy determination, information and current awareness services, banking networks, aeroplane guidance and navigation, and geo-physical exploration. Also in medicine where the complex interactions of subtle body mechanisms give rise to the side effects of modern-day drugs we find the same requirement to identify the inherent non-linear dynamic structure of the system and its associated parameters and use this increased understanding to design and synthesize improved, safer medicines.",
