        "abstract": "This paper considers three mathematical models to describe the dynamic behaviour of a large turbogenerator connected through a radial transmission line to an infinite busbar. Five different disturbances are considered, with and without a series capacitor in the transmission line, and with the turbine and generator rotors represented either as a single equivalent inertia or as a multi-inertia system interconnected by torsionally flexible shafts. The results of several case studies show that, although the simpler models yield acceptable results for certain disturbances and system configuration, they nevertheless produce totally erroneous results for other combinations of conditions.",
